<BaseLayout
  title="Darkness on the Edge of Town | Ray Weiss"
  description="Darkness on the Edge of Town. A turn-based roguelike in a present-day tri-state the game never names. Early access on itch under Conflict Simulations LLC."
>
  <main class="doc">
    <div class="doc__frame">
      <header class="page-heading">
        <nav class="eyebrow" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/conflict-simulations-llc"
            >Conflict Simulations LLC</a
          >
        </nav>
        <h1>Darkness on the Edge of Town</h1>
        <p class="dek">
          A turn-based roguelike in a present-day tri-state the game never names. Early access.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose-body">
        <p>
          Played one step at a time on a tile grid. Places, things and people start as plain
          descriptions of what they do, and earn their real names through use, a close look, or
          something you read. One readable sign gives the setting away: the New Jersey Turnpike,
          Exit 16W.
        </p>
        <p>
          You wake on a bench with an envelope in your pack. Go out from the home platform, pick a
          place by the exam it states, and come back with what you found: things to name, parts,
          food, favors and standing. Factions remember what you did. Attack or steal from someone in
          a town and the locals turn on you.
        </p>
        <p>
          Under the ordinary world, the thing in the marsh keeps everything and uses nothing. It can
          mark you, and each of the six marks deepens as you go back to the faces that gave it.
        </p>
      </div>

